* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.tif binary
*.tiff binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.zst binary

# Frozen experiment artifacts are hash-bound evidence, not source. Their
# sha256 values are recorded inside sealed receipts (protocol-freeze.json,
# selection-seal.json, lane-a-native-freeze.json, the H3 V03 seal, ...) and
# are re-verified by verify_frozen_integrity.py and verify_seal(). The
# repository-wide `* text=auto eol=lf` rule above would rewrite CRLF to LF on
# checkin, changing those bytes and silently breaking every seal that covers
# them -- measured directly: SEM-RISK-CONF-02/protocol.json hashes
# c8238f96... on disk (the value its freeze receipt records) but 38a88e5d...
# after normalization. `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion so the
# committed bytes are the sealed bytes.
research/experiments/**/*.json -text
research/experiments/**/*.py -text
research/experiments/**/*.jsonl -text
infra/runpod/v6/qualification/**/*.json -text


